  "title": "Adverbios de tiempo y de frecuencia",
  "description": "Now, today, yesterday, already, yet, always, never… con ejemplos.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Cuándo",
      "table": {
        "columns": ["Inglés", "Español", "Ejemplo", "En español"],
        "rows": [
          ["now", "ahora", "I'm busy now.", "Ahora estoy ocupado."],
          ["today", "hoy", "Today is Monday.", "Hoy es lunes."],
          ["tonight", "esta noche", "What are you doing tonight?", "¿Qué haces esta noche?"],
          ["tomorrow", "mañana", "See you tomorrow.", "Hasta mañana."],
          ["yesterday", "ayer", "I was at home yesterday.", "Ayer estuve en casa."],
          ["ago", "hace (tiempo)", "I arrived two days ago.", "Llegué hace dos días."],
          ["already", "ya", "I've already eaten.", "Ya he comido."],
          [
            "yet",
            "todavía (negativas); ya (preguntas)",
            "Have you finished yet?",
            "¿Ya has terminado?"
          ],
          [
            "still",
            "todavía, aún",
            "She still lives with her parents.",
            "Todavía vive con sus padres."
          ],
          ["just", "acabar de", "I've just arrived.", "Acabo de llegar."],
          ["soon", "pronto", "We'll be there soon.", "Llegamos pronto."],
          ["later", "más tarde", "I'll call you later.", "Te llamo luego."]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "heading": "Con qué frecuencia",
      "text": "Los adverbios de frecuencia van delante del verbo principal, pero detrás de to be: I often walk, pero I am often late.",
      "table": {
        "columns": ["Inglés", "Español", "Ejemplo", "En español"],
        "rows": [
          ["always", "siempre", "I always have breakfast.", "Siempre desayuno."],
          ["usually", "normalmente", "She usually takes the bus.", "Normalmente coge el autobús."],
          ["often", "a menudo", "We often go to the cinema.", "Vamos a menudo al cine."],
          ["sometimes", "a veces", "I sometimes cook.", "A veces cocino."],
          ["rarely", "rara vez", "He rarely watches TV.", "Rara vez ve la tele."],
          ["never", "nunca", "I never drink coffee.", "Nunca bebo café."],
          ["every day", "todos los días", "I read every day.", "Leo todos los días."]
        ]
      }
